ion/vat/vat-directive/vat-rates_en?utm_source=openai"},{"end_index":1088,"start_index":937,"title":"Electronically supplied services","type":"url_citation","url":"https://www.revenue.ie/en/vat/vat-on-services/electronic-services/vat-and-electronically-supplied-services/index.aspx?utm_source=openai"},{"end_index":1364,"start_index":1255,"title":"Revenue Ready Reckoner – Post Budget 2026","type":"url_citation","url":"https://www.revenue.ie/en/corporate/documents/statistics/ready-reckoner.pdf?utm_source=openai"}],"logprobs":[],"text":"Short answer: Yes — as of today (September 4, 2026) Ireland’s standard VAT rate is 23%, and electronically supplied (digital) services supplied to Irish consumers are taxed at that rate. ([revenue.ie](https://www.revenue.ie/en/vat/vat-rates/search-vat-rates/current-VAT-rates.aspx?utm_source=openai))\n\nA few quick caveats to check before you send the PDF:\n- If the buyer is outside Ireland (another EU country), EU place-of-supply rules generally require you to charge the customer’s local VAT rate for B2C digital services. ([taxation-customs.ec.europa.eu](https://taxation-customs.ec.europa.eu/taxation/vat/vat-directive/vat-rates_en?utm_source=openai))  \n- If the buyer is a VAT-registered business in another EU state and provides a valid VAT number, the supply may be treated as B2B (reverse charge) so you would not charge Irish VAT. See Revenue’s guidance on electronically supplied services for the registration/threshold rules. ([revenue.ie](https://www.revenue.ie/en/vat/vat-on-services/electronic-services/vat-and-electronically-supplied-services/index.aspx?utm_source=openai))\n- Recent Irish Budget/2026 changes reduced some reduced VAT rates (e.g., certain hospitality items to 9% from July 1, 2026) but did not change the 23% standard rate. ([revenue.ie](https://www.revenue.ie/en/corporate/documents/statistics/ready-reckoner.pdf?utm_source=openai))\n\nI couldn’t inspect your actual PDF (you didn’t attach it) — I relied on Revenue/EC sources above. If you tell me whether the client is in Ireland or is a VAT-registered business (and you can paste the exact wording from your pricing PDF if you want), I’ll give the exact wording you should use or a one-line update you can drop into the document.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_00aa7fe69f240c26016a9a6d8ff73c87d09186edfb23e9af93","role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message"}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"presence_penalty":0.0,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":"in_memory","reasoning":{"context":"current_turn","effort":"medium","mode":"standard","summary":null},"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"default","status":"completed","store":false,"temperature":1.0,"text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"medium"},"tool_choice":"auto","tool_usage":{"image_gen":{"input_tokens":0,"input_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"total_tokens":0},"web_search":{"num_requests":1}},"tools":[{"return_token_budget":"default","search_content_types":["text"],"search_context_size":"low","type":"web_search","user_location":{"city":null,"country":"US","region":null,"timezone":null,"type":"approximate"}}],"top_logprobs":0,"top_p":1.0,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":9415,"input_tokens_details":{"cache_write_tokens":0,"cached_tokens":4608},"output_tokens":2087,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1664},"total_tokens":11502},"user":null},"durationMs":24872.62187502347,"headers":{"access-control-expose-headers":"X-Request-ID, CF-Ray, CF-Ray","alt-svc":"h3=\":443\"; ma=86400","cf-cache-status":"DYNAMIC","cf-ray":"a35b23e1cec1312c-LAX","connection":"keep-alive","content-encoding":"gzip","content-type":"application/json","date":"Fri, 04 Sep 2026 07:04:51 GMT","openai-organization":"ben-mouqlz","openai-processing-ms":"24681","openai-project":"proj_6YFWNh4NzlKW1TydNdZL4ly2","openai-version":"2020-10-01","server":"clo